{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781226247,"nonce":"QTVsaqKHoWCgxrT03N32yX3m6Oo=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFOJ1lg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/254","origin":"github"},"title":"sidescan: wire new garmin_sidescan outputs (nadir frame in URDF, record nadir_depth, set freq params)","message":"## Summary\n\nrolker/marine_tools#35 upgraded the `garmin_sidescan` driver: `RawSonarImage.sample_rate` now carries the true per-ping, per-channel range scale, and the per-ping nadir bottom range (sub-header v1, M3-validated) is published as `sensor_msgs/Range` on `~/nadir_depth` in a dedicated `\u003cframe_id\u003e_nadir` frame (+X down, per the Range spec — distinct from the Z-down `_down` water-column frame).\n\nThree platform-side consequences on bizzy need wiring:\n\n1. **URDF**: `bizzyboat_project11/urdf/sensors/sidescan.xacro` defines `_down`/`_port`/`_starboard` links but no `_nadir` link. Add a `\u003cframe_id\u003e_nadir` frame with +X pointing down at the transducer pose, or `nadir_depth` publishes into a nonexistent frame.\n2. **Bag recording**: `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml` records `sonar_image_*` / `state` / `debug/raw*` but not `nadir_depth`. Add it (tiny: ~10 Hz `sensor_msgs/Range`).\n3. **Frequency params**: deployment bags show `ping_info.frequency = 0.0` on all sidescan channels — the per-transducer `freq_port_hz` / `freq_stbd_hz` / `freq_down_hz` params are unset in the launch config. Set them for the GCV-20 transducer (frequency is not carried in the imagery stream; see the driver README).\n\n## References\n\n- Driver change: rolker/marine_tools#35 (sample_rate from sub-header v2 + nadir_depth from v1)\n- Protocol evidence: `garmin_sidescan/docs/gcv_protocol.md` §3.1/§3.5\n- Range-frame convention: `build_nadir_range` docstring (`node.py`)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}